; divisibility is preserved by raising to a power: a|b -> a^n | b^n.
; From a|b get b = k*a; then b^n = (k*a)^n = k^n * a^n [power distributes over product], so a^n divides b^n with cofactor k^n. No induction in this proof -- it composes the (inductive) power-distributes lemma + one rewrite. A number-theoretic closure property: the divisibility relation respects exponentiation.
